Selected directory names, service subdomains, package namespaces and command
phrases give positive responses; their spelling and preceding separators matter.
Java/Android namespace responses are stronger near import keywords. Chat user headers
also respond positively. Secondary rules cover research-result references,
"This content", title labels, and small user/config/domain/first-token baselines.

The constants are rounded training summaries, not a model reconstruction.
A bounded text buffer supplies context and resets at each new document.
Unmatched tokens return zero, except for the stated baselines. This leaves
