"""Layer-1 MLP neuron 2597 (the down_proj component 2597), as a word-level program.

The component is almost exactly one hidden unit of layer 1's MLP, so its activation depends
mostly on which word the current token is. It is large and positive on a few families of
word and large and negative on others, and close to zero on almost every other token. This
program scores the current token by which family it belongs to:

  + location phrases of two or more characters, such as 上面, 下面, 里面, 之上, 之下, 之中,
    以内, 当中 (about +1), and looser place words such as 之间, 外面, 前面, 内部 (about +0.4)
  + "upon" completing a dependence phrase: based upon, depend(s|ing) upon (about +1.3)
  + Japanese polite verb endings: しま, しております, おります, いたします, まして (about +1.2)
  + contrast and purpose connectives: 但是, 想要, 使得, 对于, 是在 (about +0.6)
  - time-before and time-after words: 以前, 之前, 以往, 以后, 已经 (about -0.5)
  - list connectives and plural suffixes: 或者, 以及, 等等, 們, 们, 들 (about -0.5)

Every other token predicts 0. This is a coarse description. It explains only a small part of
the activation's variance: most of the variance sits in many rare words and in context, which
a short word list cannot capture.
"""

READS = ()

LOCATION_STRONG = {"上面", "下面", "里面", "之上", "之下", "之中", "之内", "以内", "当中", "底下"}
LOCATION_WEAK = {"之间", "之外", "前面", "外面", "内部", "旁边", "后面", "上方", "下方", "周围"}
JAPANESE_POLITE = {"まして", "しま", "しております", "おります", "いたします", "いただいて", "でしょうか"}
CONTRAST_PURPOSE = {"但是", "可是", "想要", "使得", "对于", "是在", "是一", "能够", "具有"}
BEFORE_AFTER = {"以前", "之前", "以往", "以后", "已经", "已經"}
LIST_PLURAL = {"或者", "以及", "等等", "們", "们", "들", "들이", "등"}
DEPEND_WORDS = {"based", "depend", "depends", "depending", "dependent", "reflect"}

GROUPS = (
    (LOCATION_STRONG, 1.0),
    (LOCATION_WEAK, 0.4),
    (JAPANESE_POLITE, 1.2),
    (CONTRAST_PURPOSE, 0.6),
    (BEFORE_AFTER, -0.5),
    (LIST_PLURAL, -0.5),
)


def step(carry, prefix, upstream):
